# Docker reads the ignore file from the build CONTEXT ROOT. Both build paths set
# that root to the repository root (cd.yml `context: .`, docker-compose.yml
# `context: ../..`), so this file is in force and infrastructure/docker/.dockerignore
# is never loaded. A `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` would REPLACE this file
# outright, so none may be created beside infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile.

# Patterns match relative to that root, so a bare `node_modules/` would not match
# src/backend/node_modules: the backend artifacts need the recursive `**/` form,
# while entries that genuinely sit at the root are written bare.

# src/backend/package.json, src/backend/package-lock.json and the application
# sources are deliberately NOT excluded; both image stages read them from the context.

**/node_modules
**/coverage
**/*.log

**/jest.config.js
**/nodemon.json
**/.eslintrc.js
**/.prettierrc

# `**/.env` matches the literal name only, hence `**/.env.example`
**/.env
**/.env.example

src/backend/tests
.git
docs/
infrastructure/
